We tend to use rupnu when talking about a specific kind of money, i.e. {lo
merko rupnu} =3D {lo meryru'u} =3D "US$", {lo brito rupnu} =3D {lo ritru'u}=
 =3D
"UK=A3", {lo ponjo rupnu} =3D {lo ponru'u} =3D "JP=A5", etc.

When talking about generic context-evident money, we tend to use jdini.

For example:
{lo do jgari be lo jdini ca klani ma}
"How much cash do you have on you?"

There's probably more elegant ways to say the above in Lojban, I was being
quick, not poetic.


